nding mosul where a lot of these  displaced people come from  now here the pace of rebuilding is slow  but in those smaller towns and villages  it's practically non-existent most of  the rebuilding effort seems to be  focused on the unesco heritage site  the al-nuri mosque the former  headquarters of isil  but with few homes even remotely livable  who might go to the rebuilt mosque  is under question if families move back  without homes and jobs  it will make the situation worse they  will beg in the streets  and this will worsen the already bad  economic situation  most of these families are eligible for  compensation  but few families have received anything  out of the 73 000 families who have  asked for help to rebuild  and move home since 2018 only 2 000  have received help according to human  rights groups  for thousands of people the camps are  their only option but  there are a few left and the pressure to  shut them is growing every day  imran khan al jazeera mosul
 

